title: Organized Labor Under Threat
subtitle: Proposal for a united labor front between the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> unions.
view-if: chancellor = "Staal" and gnu_formed and staal_post_time >= 6
new-page: true
priority: 2
tags: event
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/beauty_of_labor.jpg

= Organized Labor Under Threat

We have observed extensive infiltration of Staal's supporters into the leadership of the Greater Worker's Guild, the <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span>, and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">liberal</span> Free Guilds—with the rank-and-file of all three even more inclined to back him.

In response, a proposal for a united labor front—bringing together our Greater Worker's Guild, the <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> GcG formerly led by Sedgewick, and the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Hirsch-Duncker</span> liberal unions under Hollis Lindell—has been floated by figures like our Emory Lespan and the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>'s Aldwin Stilling.

The hope is that such unity will allow organized labor to resist coercion from Staal’s government and secure a stronger position within the corporatist order he has been promoting, should it come to that.

- @schleicher_2: A united labor front is formed!
- @schleicher_3: Negotiations stall.

@schleicher_2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if staal_marcher_influence >= 6: Staal uses his influence within the Greater Worker's Guild to block further negotiations. ?][? if labor_dissent >= 40 or unions_independent: Labor dissent is too high. ?][? if unionist_relation < 40 or (unionist_relation < 60 and unionist_in_gov): We lack the adequate relations with the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>. ?]
choose-if: staal_marcher_influence < 6 and (unionist_relation >= 40 or (unionist_relation >= 60 and unionist_in_gov)) and labor_dissent < 40 and not unions_independent

Negotiations have progressed, but one major obstacle remains: the Greater Worker's Guild’s continued commitment to <span style="color: #9B0000;">Vaelism</span>, setting it apart from the other unions that now advocate for class collaboration. The question stands—do we stay silent on this point, for the sake of unity?

- @schleicher_2_pro
- @schleicher_3: Negotiations stall.

@schleicher_2_pro
title: Go along with the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>'s proposal.
unavailable-subtitle: Our party doesn't support this course of action.
choose-if: labor_strength >= center_strength + left_strength
on-arrival: {!
Q.united_labor = 1

Q.pro_republic += 8;

Q.unionist_relation += 15;
Q.ddp_relation += 15;
Q.lvp_relation += 5;
Q.ddp_left += 5;
Q.lvp_left += 2;

Q.left_dissent += 50;
Q.center_dissent += 20;
Q.labor_dissent -= 20;

Q.commons_gnu -= 8;
Q.commons_lvp += 2;
Q.commons_ddp += 2;
Q.commons_unionist += 2;
Q.commons_marcher += 6;

Q.disfavored_gnu -= 6;
Q.disfavored_marcher += 6;
!}

The unification of the labor unions has complicated Staal's efforts to divide and conquer, depriving him of the option to play the more moderate unions against the Greater Worker's Guild. We have also agreed to coordinate unified action in response to any offensive measures his government may attempt in the coming months.

@schleicher_3
on-arrival: {!
Q.commons_staal_bonus += 1;

Q.commons_unionist -= 2;
Q.commons_gnu += 2;
!}

Without coordination among the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> unions, Staal has moved quickly to strike separate deals with the more right-leaning organizations. The Clerks' Guild, the conservative white-collar union, has been the first to pledge loyalty to the "new state," joined by the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Hirsch-Duncker</span> unions—too marginal to wield real leverage anyway.

The <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> unions have been cozying up to Staal for months[? if unionist_in_gov:, and Sedgewick's entry into government has only accelerated these talks of cooperation between his cabinet and the unionists.?][? if not unionist_in_gov:, though they remain broadly wary of Staal and his true intentions.?] Their advocacy for a "pluralistic" model, where unions retain formal autonomy within a corporatist the Commonwealth, has only made Staal’s task easier.

[? if staal_marcher_influence >= 6: Staal has also been quietly cultivating allies within the Greater Worker's Guild itself. Voices calling for the rejection of <span style="color: #9B0000;">Vaelism</span> and a break with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> are growing louder by the day. Damn it. ?]